From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:21:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): ask for a project when starting a new session
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A project carries the settings a new session needs (host, workspace,
agent, model, worktree), but every "new session" entry point opens a
plain composer, so filing a session in its project and getting those
defaults is an extra, easily forgotten step.

When projects exist, the new-session hotkey, the sidebar's New session
links (also reached from the phone drawer) and the palette's New chat,
in either palette, now open a "Start a new session in…" picker: No
project first, then every project, filtered by name as you type.
Picking one opens /?project=<name>; Escape stays on the page. Modified
clicks on the links still open the composer in a new tab, and Settings
> General > Sessions has a switch to turn the prompt off, with its
Settings-search entry.

The prompt is its own picker rather than a mode of the command palette,
so it is the same under the classic palette and the QuickPick one. It
and the palette replace each other instead of stacking. On a project's
home page none of the entry points ask: the session starts in that
project, in the home's composer over the board as its New session
button does (on phones, /?project=<name>). The picker is for places
with no project in view; on the composer already filed under a
project, that project starts highlighted.

The picker is offered while the project list is still loading and
steps aside for the plain composer when the list fails or comes back
empty. Below the md breakpoint it is a bottom sheet instead, whose
missing search field keeps the keyboard down: a grab handle, "Start a
new session in", then No project and every project as 48px rows. The
sheet is a small controlled BottomSheet primitive on the Radix dialog
(the UI kit had none).

Browser tests that click New session and expect the composer turn the
prompt off (omnigent:new-chat-project-prompt=false). The feature map
documents the prompt.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/new-chat-project-prompt
(https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/pull/11397); drop this copy
once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
